          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Reading this page",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#020617"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Model \u2014 second-purchase propensity: probability a first-time buyer places a 2nd order within 180 days. Churn risk = the Low band.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#475569"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "A ranker, not a classifier (ROC-AUC \u2014 0.58). 97% buy once, so signal is faint, but the ranking holds: High-propensity buyers return at 4.9% vs 2.1% for Low (2.3x) against a 3.0% base.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#475569"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Top drivers (SHAP): product category, delivery-vs-estimate gap, installments, first-order value, purchase month \u2014 first-order experience and basket economics carry what signal exists.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#475569"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Action: aim the second-purchase nudge at the High band (same spend, ~2x return rate) and protect first-order delivery \u2014 it ties to the late-delivery penalty in Fulfillment (Case 4) and Experimentation (Case 6).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#020617"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
